From 688a02a5556770593cc2666bd8042e4806e8dcc0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhanpeng He <zhanpeng@stanford.edu>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:18:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add left-hand Ditto leader: mirrored URDF, hand config,
 viewer launcher

- retargeting/assets/ditto_left_leader/: mirror of ditto_3f_leader across
  the palm plane (x = 0), middle finger dropped. Generated by the new
  retargeting/mirror_urdf.py (joint axes flipped as pseudo-vectors so the
  same q gives the mirror pose; meshes reflected). thumb_joint_2 stays
  fixed as in the source model; the physical 3-motor thumb bracket has the
  same reach, so the kinematics are unchanged. See its README.md.
- conf/hand_config/ditto_left_leader_only.yaml: 6-motor leader-only chain
  (111, 112, 114, 121, 122, 123), all direction -1, zero_position
  calibrated against the mirrored model on 2026-10-30.
- viz/view_left_leader.py: viewer launcher that binds viser to 127.0.0.1,
  pads a partial motor chain to the full URDF q, swaps in the left model
  with --left, and adds live zero-offset sliders that print zero_position
  values for the yaml.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BJ6GavYdBGei2pWbgBp6gN
